{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Curse for me.</b> A directive form from doubled-action [verbs] lacking the doubling letter; likewise קבה לי. And behold, קוב is on the pattern of שמור, while קבה לי lacks the heh, on the pattern of שכב רכב צלח." "<b>Strike him.</b> A verb [noun?]; and there is no objection on account of its having a heh, for behold, כמוהו לכלה הפשע is like it." "<b>May be defeated.</b> The vav replaces the concealed [root letter] in place of the dagesh, which is under the doubling letter, like על כמון יושב. And it would not be like it from that binyan on account of the guttural letter, as is the rule."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra calls נכה a שם הפועל (verbal noun/infinitive), though it functions here as an imperative; the comparison to לכלה הפשע (Micah 7:18) supports reading it as a nominal form used with directive force."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:54.027115383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}